1
00:00:04,330 --> 00:00:05,670
And here we are!

2
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:07,630
This will be our new home
and workshop

3
00:00:07,710 --> 00:00:09,580
for the next two months,
to be precise.

4
00:00:09,670 --> 00:00:13,670
Um! Mister Collins, this is what
the church provided us?

5
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:16,040
Indeed they did, and at no cost!

6
00:00:16,130 --> 00:00:17,880
Lewiston isn't far from here

7
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:19,880
and we'll be able
to secure as much space

8
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:21,460
as we need to do our work.

9
00:00:22,130 --> 00:00:24,460
Something wrong?
You seem troubled.

10
00:00:24,540 --> 00:00:26,830
This is a charming castle,
if you ask me!

11
00:00:26,920 --> 00:00:30,000
I suppose it has a rustic
appeal, in a sense

12
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:31,380
but it looks a bit...

13
00:00:31,460 --> 00:00:34,460
♪

14
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:45,580
- It looks a bit haunted.
- Eh?

15
00:00:45,670 --> 00:00:48,210
Challe! Don't say
such strange things!

16
00:00:48,290 --> 00:00:50,880
[GLEN]
I see. Holly Leaf Castle.

17
00:00:51,420 --> 00:00:53,880
I wondered why they didn't tell
us the name of our new space

18
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:55,330
now I have my answer.

19
00:00:55,710 --> 00:00:57,080
Holly Leaf Castle?

20
00:00:57,170 --> 00:00:59,500
Do you know something
about this place, Mister Glen?

21
00:00:59,580 --> 00:01:01,170
Not everyone knows the story,

22
00:01:01,250 --> 00:01:03,290
it's quite infamous amongst
those who do.

23
00:01:03,790 --> 00:01:06,580
Fifteen years ago,
the royal family of Millsland

24
00:01:06,670 --> 00:01:07,920
faced an insurrection

25
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,130
started by a branch family,
House Chamber.

26
00:01:11,210 --> 00:01:14,040
It's commonly referred to
as the Chambers Rebellion.

27
00:01:14,130 --> 00:01:16,960
The battle ended in
House Millsland's victory.

28
00:01:18,080 --> 00:01:19,920
And so, House Chamber
and their followers

29
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:21,420
were put to death.

30
00:01:22,170 --> 00:01:25,170
This castle was associated
with House Chamber.

31
00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:27,670
They killed everyone here?

32
00:01:27,750 --> 00:01:29,000
That's a tragic story,

33
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:31,290
but is that reason enough
to withhold the name?

34
00:01:31,380 --> 00:01:32,830
It's not like
the place is really...

35
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:35,420
Oh, but it is! It's haunted!

36
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:37,670
I bet it's positively brimming
with ghosts!

37
00:01:37,750 --> 00:01:39,000
[screams]

38
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:40,880
Stop it that's not funny!

39
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:43,830
I've heard strange tales
but they're just rumors.

40
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:44,790
Whatever the case,

41
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:48,130
we're doing this for the sake
of the Holy Beginnings Festival.

42
00:01:48,210 --> 00:01:50,790
Let's not question
the church's generosity.

43
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:52,830
"Strange tales" he says.

44
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:55,040
Does sound a bit foreboding,
doesn't it?

45
00:01:55,670 --> 00:01:59,290
Hmm! I'm the Head of Artisans!

46
00:01:59,380 --> 00:02:02,040
I can't afford
to be scared by ghost stories!

47
00:02:02,130 --> 00:02:03,630
Now that we've been chosen
in the selection,

48
00:02:03,710 --> 00:02:05,670
we have to fulfill our promise!

49
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:08,500
We'll create
beautiful sugar confections

50
00:02:08,580 --> 00:02:10,580
worthy of
the Holy Beginnings Festival!

51
00:02:11,460 --> 00:02:13,830
♪

52
00:03:41,750 --> 00:03:42,750
Huh!

53
00:03:42,830 --> 00:03:46,920
♪

54
00:03:53,420 --> 00:03:56,170
It's spacious enough
but it doesn't seem very clean.

55
00:03:56,250 --> 00:03:58,290
We're supposed to sleep
in this place?

56
00:03:58,380 --> 00:04:00,130
I thought
the Holy Beginnings Festival

57
00:04:00,210 --> 00:04:02,630
was meant to invite good fortune
for the coming year.

58
00:04:02,710 --> 00:04:05,040
If I was good fortune
and I saw this place,

59
00:04:05,130 --> 00:04:06,790
I would turn around
and go the other way.

60
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:09,000
[ELLIOTT]
All right! All right!

61
00:04:09,080 --> 00:04:11,000
That's enough complaining
for today!

62
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:13,290
We have all our supplies,
so let's get to work!

63
00:04:13,380 --> 00:04:14,830
[ANNE]
Uh. He's right.

64
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:17,920
No excuses!
And no being scared, either!

65
00:04:18,630 --> 00:04:19,880
[screams]

66
00:04:19,960 --> 00:04:22,000
[CHALLE] This is likely
the work of House Millsland.

67
00:04:23,040 --> 00:04:23,920
[ANNE]
Challe.

68
00:04:24,790 --> 00:04:26,460
[CHALLE]
Look closely.

69
00:04:26,540 --> 00:04:28,420
They didn't just cut the faces,

70
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:30,460
swords and decorations
are gone as well.

71
00:04:31,170 --> 00:04:33,750
I think we can assume
what their target was,

72
00:04:33,830 --> 00:04:35,330
the crest of House Chamber.

73
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,670
[ANNE] Then it must
have been everywhere.

74
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:41,040
[CHALLE] To House Millsland,
the crest of House Chamber

75
00:04:41,130 --> 00:04:44,130
became taboo after they started
the rebellion.

76
00:04:44,210 --> 00:04:46,710
They must have wanted
to eradicate every trace of it.

77
00:04:47,380 --> 00:04:48,290
Uh!

78
00:04:48,380 --> 00:04:50,040
[KING]
I was wondering, Elliott.

79
00:04:50,580 --> 00:04:51,960
What's happened to Bridget?

80
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:55,040
She said she'd come here later,
so I gave her some money

81
00:04:55,130 --> 00:04:56,830
and asked her
to hire a carriage.

82
00:04:56,920 --> 00:04:58,130
I'm sure she's fine.

83
00:04:59,130 --> 00:05:01,290
[NADIR] That's cold,
coming from her fiance!

84
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:03,000
Hmm!

85
00:05:03,630 --> 00:05:06,130
[ORLAND] Whatever's happening
with her doesn't concern us now.

86
00:05:06,210 --> 00:05:08,500
Time to move your feet
instead of your mouths.

87
00:05:16,630 --> 00:05:18,710
Hmm! [coughs]

88
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:27,630
It's just messy, not haunted.
Now, focus, it's time to clean!

89
00:05:30,420 --> 00:05:32,040
[HERBERT]
Silver Sugar Master.

90
00:05:32,130 --> 00:05:33,250
Uh!

91
00:05:33,330 --> 00:05:37,210
♪

92
00:05:37,290 --> 00:05:39,460
No, I'm just imagining things.

93
00:05:40,500 --> 00:05:41,580
[HERBERT]
I'm glad you're here.

94
00:05:41,670 --> 00:05:42,670
[screams]

95
00:05:47,540 --> 00:05:50,750
Hmm! [screams]

96
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:52,920
- Something wrong?
- I heard one!

97
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:55,710
- A gh-gh-gh-gh-gh. Ghost!
- Let's calm down.

98
00:05:55,790 --> 00:05:56,920
You know there
aren't any ghosts here.

99
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:57,960
But there was a voice!

100
00:05:58,040 --> 00:06:00,080
Someone said
"I'm glad you're here," I swear!

101
00:06:00,170 --> 00:06:01,960
Stop. You're hearing things,
that's all.

102
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:04,580
You may think I'm crazy,
but it's true! I've been cursed!

103
00:06:04,670 --> 00:06:06,170
I've been cursed
by the House Chamber

104
00:06:06,250 --> 00:06:08,420
and they'll haunt me 'til
I'm dead if you don't save me!

105
00:06:08,500 --> 00:06:10,580
Then should I kiss you?

106
00:06:10,670 --> 00:06:13,580
Uh! What did you just say?
A kiss?

107
00:06:13,670 --> 00:06:14,920
Are you still scared?

108
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:18,750
Uh! No, I'm sorry.
I was just being silly.

109
00:06:18,830 --> 00:06:22,080
[ELLIOTT] Say, Anne!
Can you spare a minute?

110
00:06:22,170 --> 00:06:24,290
It sounds like
I have work to do. Bye, then.

111
00:06:29,750 --> 00:06:30,960
Uh!

112
00:06:35,080 --> 00:06:37,330
It appears that our ghost
leaves footprints.

113
00:06:38,130 --> 00:06:40,130
[ELLIOTT] We're done
bringing the supplies in!

114
00:06:40,210 --> 00:06:42,250
Could you look over the layout
of our workspace?

115
00:06:42,330 --> 00:06:43,790
[ANNE]
Yes, of course!

116
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:46,420
Hmm!

117
00:06:49,380 --> 00:06:51,080
Why isn't this painting dirty?

118
00:06:53,710 --> 00:06:55,580
Let's leave things here
for today.

119
00:06:55,670 --> 00:06:57,540
Get some rest
and we'll start work tomorrow.

120
00:07:01,710 --> 00:07:03,380
Huh? Sleep in here?

121
00:07:03,460 --> 00:07:05,750
I just feel uneasy somehow.

122
00:07:05,830 --> 00:07:07,920
I know that there are enough
rooms for everyone,

123
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,500
but I don't want to be alone.

124
00:07:09,580 --> 00:07:12,290
Sorry, Mithril Lid Pod,
but can you please stay?

125
00:07:12,380 --> 00:07:15,380
[MITHRIL] Well, it's not
that I mind exactly but--

126
00:07:15,460 --> 00:07:16,330
But what?

127
00:07:16,420 --> 00:07:18,710
I think you should ask
Challe fenn Challe to do this

128
00:07:18,790 --> 00:07:20,880
sort of thing for you,
instead of me.

129
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:21,790
Really.

130
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:24,460
Ah! But it's far too
embarrassing

131
00:07:24,540 --> 00:07:26,500
and I'm certain
he'd make fun of me!

132
00:07:26,580 --> 00:07:28,250
You are such a fool!

133
00:07:28,330 --> 00:07:30,330
Keep saying things like that
and your romance will be dead

134
00:07:30,420 --> 00:07:31,670
before it starts!

135
00:07:31,750 --> 00:07:33,540
Love is like a fairy, you know!

136
00:07:33,630 --> 00:07:36,460
It can be born
from anything in any situation!

137
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:39,170
All right,
I'll ask him for you right now!

138
00:07:39,250 --> 00:07:40,920
- [laughs]
- What? No! Come back here!

139
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,330
I did not agree to that!

140
00:07:42,420 --> 00:07:45,710
I'm trying to repay your favor!
Why are you getting in my way?

141
00:07:45,790 --> 00:07:47,920
Because that wouldn't repay
my favor at all,

142
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,380
- I'm telling you! Stop it!
- Of course it will

143
00:07:49,460 --> 00:07:50,750
- Stay with me!
- [CHALLE] Why are you yelling?

144
00:07:51,460 --> 00:07:53,500
Challe fenn Challe!
Perfect timing!

145
00:07:53,580 --> 00:07:55,250
- Anne wants you to sleep...
- [yells]

146
00:07:56,710 --> 00:08:00,500
I'm sorry, Challe. There's
nothing wrong. Did we wake you?

147
00:08:00,580 --> 00:08:03,080
There's nothing?
And You're certain?

148
00:08:03,170 --> 00:08:05,540
[ANNE]
Um, is there something?

149
00:08:05,630 --> 00:08:07,580
Something violet.
Can't say what.

150
00:08:07,670 --> 00:08:09,500
You're not joking, are you?

151
00:08:09,580 --> 00:08:11,540
What's going on
with this castle?

152
00:08:11,630 --> 00:08:13,380
I knew this place was haunted!
I want to see!

153
00:08:13,460 --> 00:08:16,630
Whether ghosts are the issue
here or not, be careful.

154
00:08:16,710 --> 00:08:18,080
[creaks]

155
00:08:18,170 --> 00:08:20,670
- Hey, come back!
- [Mithril imitates howl]

156
00:08:20,750 --> 00:08:22,460
You can't say all those
scary things

157
00:08:22,540 --> 00:08:23,830
and then just walk away!

158
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:24,920
How awful.

159
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,580
And whose fault is that, huh?

160
00:08:26,670 --> 00:08:28,130
You should have been bold
and asked him

161
00:08:28,210 --> 00:08:29,790
to sleep with you! Honestly!

162
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:32,250
Those are completely
different matters!

163
00:08:33,040 --> 00:08:35,960
Now please, will you do
as I asked before?

164
00:08:36,040 --> 00:08:38,380
Just stay here
and sleep with me.

165
00:08:38,460 --> 00:08:41,750
Well, if you insist.
I don't mind.

166
00:08:43,500 --> 00:08:45,830
[birds chirping]

167
00:08:45,920 --> 00:08:48,080
[creaks]

168
00:08:48,170 --> 00:08:51,080
Hmm! Daana, how is
Mister Glen doing today?

169
00:08:51,170 --> 00:08:52,830
Same as before, it seems.

170
00:08:52,920 --> 00:08:55,040
He ate all of his breakfast,
so that's good.

171
00:08:57,500 --> 00:08:58,880
[ANNE]
Good morning, everyone.

172
00:08:58,960 --> 00:09:01,080
[yawns]

173
00:09:01,460 --> 00:09:03,880
Huh! Not you too!

174
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:06,330
You look just like Orland.
Couldn't sleep?

175
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:09,420
Uh! Seems like there's something
wrong with the lock to my room.

176
00:09:09,500 --> 00:09:10,960
I kept closing it,

177
00:09:11,040 --> 00:09:13,040
but then the door
would open itself again.

178
00:09:13,130 --> 00:09:15,460
I know what you mean,
my room's the same.

179
00:09:15,540 --> 00:09:17,960
- Mine, too!
- Mine as well.

180
00:09:18,040 --> 00:09:20,460
I heard doors opening
and closing all night long,

181
00:09:20,540 --> 00:09:22,080
so I couldn't sleep a wink.

182
00:09:22,170 --> 00:09:24,080
I wonder
what could be causing this?

183
00:09:24,170 --> 00:09:25,880
Say, that reminds me.

184
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:27,960
Huh! Since you couldn't sleep,

185
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:30,500
did any of you happen to see
a violet-colored something

186
00:09:30,580 --> 00:09:31,670
or other last night?

187
00:09:31,750 --> 00:09:33,000
Not that I recall.

188
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:35,500
Is there something
we should know about?

189
00:09:36,130 --> 00:09:39,420
We have a ghost.
It's been confirmed.

190
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:41,080
But never fear, my friends

191
00:09:41,170 --> 00:09:42,880
for the magnificent
Mithril Lid Pod

192
00:09:42,960 --> 00:09:44,540
will easily dispose of...

193
00:09:44,630 --> 00:09:48,420
Stop jumping to conclusions.
I never said it was a ghost.

194
00:09:48,500 --> 00:09:50,630
Well, I don't know much
about ghosts,

195
00:09:50,710 --> 00:09:52,040
so I'll leave this to you.

196
00:09:52,130 --> 00:09:53,830
[shouts]
The glory shall be mine alone!

197
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:56,670
This I vow! You can just
stand back and watch, Challe!

198
00:09:56,750 --> 00:09:59,460
With that matter settled,
let's move on to our work.

199
00:09:59,540 --> 00:10:02,250
First off, I am sure that
our esteemed Head of Artisans

200
00:10:02,330 --> 00:10:04,880
has an idea of how the project
needs to be managed.

201
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:06,170
Mm-hm.

202
00:10:06,250 --> 00:10:08,000
We have our concept set

203
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:10,540
but all these confections need
to be a lot larger

204
00:10:10,630 --> 00:10:12,630
than what we made
for the selection.

205
00:10:12,710 --> 00:10:15,040
Remember, we're decorating
the entire church.

206
00:10:15,130 --> 00:10:17,080
So, not only
will the crystals be large,

207
00:10:17,170 --> 00:10:19,330
we'll also need
a tremendous number of them.

208
00:10:19,960 --> 00:10:22,290
Orland and King will be
in charge of kneading.

209
00:10:22,380 --> 00:10:24,250
King will also
handle the coloring.

210
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:28,330
As for the others,
myself included,

211
00:10:28,420 --> 00:10:31,210
we'll make snow crystals
and handle construction.

212
00:10:31,290 --> 00:10:33,250
Now, as for the schedule
we should...

213
00:10:33,330 --> 00:10:35,040
- Uh?
- [door creaks]

214
00:10:35,130 --> 00:10:39,170
[HUGH] Well, well. What an
interesting workspace this is!

215
00:10:39,250 --> 00:10:42,290
Certainly a creative choice,
coming from the church.

216
00:10:42,380 --> 00:10:44,210
- [ANNE] It's Hugh!
- Hello!

217
00:10:44,290 --> 00:10:47,540
Been quite a while,
Miss Silver Sugar Master.

218
00:10:49,250 --> 00:10:51,460
[ELLIOTT]
An inspection you say?

219
00:10:52,040 --> 00:10:54,460
[HUGH] This is standard
practice every year.

220
00:10:54,540 --> 00:10:57,170
A job performed
by the Silver Sugar Viscount.

221
00:10:57,250 --> 00:10:59,210
It's a commission
from the religious leaders.

222
00:10:59,920 --> 00:11:01,830
It's to ascertain the progress
of the pieces

223
00:11:01,920 --> 00:11:04,330
and ensure that your workmanship
is up to their standard.

224
00:11:05,130 --> 00:11:07,040
That's not the only safety
precaution they take,

225
00:11:07,130 --> 00:11:08,210
by the way.

226
00:11:09,170 --> 00:11:11,380
They also request backup
sugar confections

227
00:11:11,460 --> 00:11:12,790
from the Mercury Workshop.

228
00:11:13,670 --> 00:11:15,960
They hope that you can meet
your obligations

229
00:11:16,040 --> 00:11:18,500
but if you cannot
then the backup confections

230
00:11:18,580 --> 00:11:20,210
will be displayed instead.

231
00:11:20,290 --> 00:11:23,170
Naturally,
you will not be compensated.

232
00:11:23,250 --> 00:11:26,920
Uh! Did you know all this?
That's not good!

233
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:29,500
Since our school has never
participated in the selection,

234
00:11:29,580 --> 00:11:31,130
it's news to me, too.

235
00:11:31,210 --> 00:11:32,750
No need to worry!

236
00:11:32,830 --> 00:11:35,040
As long as you fulfill your end
of the obligation,

237
00:11:35,130 --> 00:11:37,580
everything will proceed
exactly as planned.

238
00:11:37,670 --> 00:11:39,080
By the way, Anne,

239
00:11:39,170 --> 00:11:40,960
I've heard all
about your exploits!

240
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:43,880
Pulling these young talents
together, winning the selection,

241
00:11:43,960 --> 00:11:45,500
and even getting Challe back!

242
00:11:46,380 --> 00:11:48,380
And good job, Elliott.

243
00:11:48,460 --> 00:11:50,750
You recognized Anne's
potential right away.

244
00:11:50,830 --> 00:11:53,380
She's a great asset
to the Paige Workshop.

245
00:11:53,460 --> 00:11:55,790
You've got a sharp eye
and dubious morals.

246
00:11:55,880 --> 00:11:57,500
A fine pair indeed.

247
00:11:57,580 --> 00:11:59,960
Your lavish praise
humbles me most painfully.

248
00:12:00,040 --> 00:12:01,960
[HUGH]
I have high hopes.

249
00:12:02,040 --> 00:12:04,540
Well then, I'll go pay
my respects to the master

250
00:12:04,630 --> 00:12:06,330
of the school and be on my way.

251
00:12:06,420 --> 00:12:07,790
Where is Glen's room?

252
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:08,920
[ELLIOTT]
Come with me.

253
00:12:09,500 --> 00:12:10,540
I forgot to say,

254
00:12:10,630 --> 00:12:13,630
my inspections will always
be unannounced.

255
00:12:13,710 --> 00:12:15,880
I'll appear without warning,
as I did today.

256
00:12:16,420 --> 00:12:18,750
So, don't relax
just because I'm not around.

257
00:12:18,830 --> 00:12:19,830
[ALL]
Hmm!

258
00:12:22,170 --> 00:12:24,710
Now that all that's over with,
are we ready to start work?

259
00:12:24,790 --> 00:12:25,790
[ALL]
Yes!

260
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:29,330
♪

261
00:12:36,540 --> 00:12:39,210
[ELLIOTT]
All this beautiful silver sugar.

262
00:12:39,290 --> 00:12:40,420
Ah!

263
00:12:42,460 --> 00:12:45,080
Are you helping
or just watching us?

264
00:12:45,170 --> 00:12:47,750
Would you even accept my aid
if I offered it?

265
00:12:47,830 --> 00:12:49,500
Knowing how much work
we have ahead of us,

266
00:12:49,580 --> 00:12:51,670
you shouldn't be scowling at me.

267
00:12:51,750 --> 00:12:53,670
Try asking nicely!
I might be a big help!

268
00:12:53,750 --> 00:12:56,040
A massive hindrance more like.

269
00:12:56,330 --> 00:12:58,040
Can't we have a normal workday?

270
00:12:58,130 --> 00:13:00,040
And a quiet one,
if you don't mind.

271
00:13:00,130 --> 00:13:01,750
I don't need more distractions.

272
00:13:01,830 --> 00:13:03,210
As you wish, then!

273
00:13:03,290 --> 00:13:05,960
♪

274
00:13:10,580 --> 00:13:12,460
[ANNE]
His work is amazing!

275
00:13:12,540 --> 00:13:15,040
He really is
a silver sugar master!

276
00:13:15,130 --> 00:13:19,710
♪

277
00:13:33,170 --> 00:13:35,040
[creaks]

278
00:13:35,130 --> 00:13:36,040
Uh!

279
00:13:38,750 --> 00:13:41,540
♪

280
00:13:42,500 --> 00:13:43,670
Uh!

281
00:13:46,080 --> 00:13:48,460
[ANNE]
A fairy? Who is that?

282
00:13:49,630 --> 00:13:50,750
How lovely.

283
00:13:56,080 --> 00:13:57,290
Oh, Miss Bridget.

284
00:13:58,210 --> 00:14:00,250
[BRIDGET]
I was told to come, so I came.

285
00:14:00,880 --> 00:14:02,500
I trust you've no objections.

286
00:14:02,580 --> 00:14:05,170
Elliott, let me introduce you.

287
00:14:05,250 --> 00:14:08,500
This is my companion fairy.
I purchased him recently.

288
00:14:09,210 --> 00:14:12,080
My name is Gladus.
It's a pleasure to meet you.

289
00:14:12,170 --> 00:14:13,460
I hope all is well.

290
00:14:13,540 --> 00:14:15,210
What is this, Bridget?

291
00:14:15,290 --> 00:14:17,460
Why did you go
and get another fairy,

292
00:14:17,540 --> 00:14:19,420
especially after
what just occurred.

293
00:14:19,830 --> 00:14:22,330
If you're referring to my Father
taking Challe's wing,

294
00:14:22,420 --> 00:14:24,630
that only happened
because I restrained him.

295
00:14:24,710 --> 00:14:26,960
I won't do the same thing
to this fairy.

296
00:14:28,750 --> 00:14:30,880
I've allowed Gladus his freedom.

297
00:14:30,960 --> 00:14:33,330
That solves this issue,
does it not?

298
00:14:33,750 --> 00:14:35,920
You're doing this to spite
Mister Glen, aren't you?

299
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,670
[gasps]

300
00:14:37,750 --> 00:14:41,290
I'm simply doing what I want,
nothing less and nothing more!

301
00:14:41,380 --> 00:14:42,880
Why are you butting in now?

302
00:14:43,500 --> 00:14:45,380
Usually,
you're so indifferent to me.

303
00:14:45,460 --> 00:14:47,330
Listen, Miss Bridget.

304
00:14:47,420 --> 00:14:50,000
Whatever it is,
I do not want to hear it!

305
00:14:50,080 --> 00:14:51,420
Apologies,

306
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:53,420
but is there some issue
with my being here,

307
00:14:53,500 --> 00:14:54,460
Miss Bridget?

308
00:14:54,540 --> 00:14:56,500
No issue whatsoever.

309
00:14:56,580 --> 00:14:59,670
I'll be more than happy to tell
father about Gladus myself.

310
00:14:59,750 --> 00:15:00,880
Show me to him.

311
00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:02,830
♪

312
00:15:02,920 --> 00:15:04,040
Hm?

313
00:15:04,130 --> 00:15:05,080
[sighs]

314
00:15:05,830 --> 00:15:07,710
His heart might just give out.

315
00:15:07,790 --> 00:15:09,710
Let's break it to him nice
and easy.

316
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:13,290
I'll go with you, all right?
This way.

317
00:15:13,380 --> 00:15:16,420
♪

318
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:21,790
He's a precious stone
just like you,

319
00:15:21,880 --> 00:15:23,170
right, Challe fenn Challe?

320
00:15:23,250 --> 00:15:24,380
Is he an old friend?

321
00:15:25,080 --> 00:15:26,710
That's Challe fenn Challe?

322
00:15:27,630 --> 00:15:28,670
It can't be.

323
00:15:29,580 --> 00:15:31,170
[CHALLE]
Is there a problem?

324
00:15:31,250 --> 00:15:33,670
Pardon. It's nothing.

325
00:15:36,170 --> 00:15:37,420
[ANNE]
You know him?

326
00:15:37,500 --> 00:15:38,750
I've never met him.

327
00:15:38,830 --> 00:15:40,040
It's so strange.

328
00:15:40,130 --> 00:15:42,290
I'm sure that guy was born
from a precious stone,

329
00:15:42,380 --> 00:15:44,750
but I can't figure out
which one at all.

330
00:15:44,830 --> 00:15:46,170
I'm usually really good
at guessing

331
00:15:46,250 --> 00:15:48,540
what objects other fairies
came from too.

332
00:15:48,830 --> 00:15:50,880
I would assume it was opal.

333
00:15:50,960 --> 00:15:53,330
It reflects different colors
in different light.

334
00:15:54,080 --> 00:15:55,670
The picture of ambiguity.

335
00:15:56,040 --> 00:15:57,040
Ambiguity.

336
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:59,920
You've been dawdling here
for quite some time,

337
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,000
Miss Head of Artisans.

338
00:16:01,080 --> 00:16:03,130
Oh, I'm sorry!
I'll be right there!

339
00:16:06,330 --> 00:16:09,250
I'm afraid Elliot won't be
helping us for a while.

340
00:16:09,330 --> 00:16:11,250
If he's dealing
with family affairs,

341
00:16:11,330 --> 00:16:12,920
he'll be in no state to work.

342
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:13,960
You saw that?

343
00:16:14,290 --> 00:16:15,580
[huffs]

344
00:16:15,670 --> 00:16:17,170
Whatever happens between them,

345
00:16:17,250 --> 00:16:19,170
we can't allow this
to slow us down.

346
00:16:19,750 --> 00:16:22,290
You're right.
Let's work hard 'til nightfall.

347
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:25,380
[crickets chirping]

348
00:16:25,460 --> 00:16:27,330
[clinking]

349
00:16:31,960 --> 00:16:33,420
Ah, it's a ghost!

350
00:16:33,500 --> 00:16:36,040
Run away! Ah!

351
00:16:41,420 --> 00:16:43,380
Wait. That's Miss Bridget.

352
00:16:43,460 --> 00:16:46,250
♪

353
00:16:46,330 --> 00:16:48,540
[GLEN] You need
to stop acting like a child!

354
00:16:48,630 --> 00:16:50,170
You brought that fairy in here

355
00:16:50,250 --> 00:16:51,790
just to attract attention
from people

356
00:16:51,880 --> 00:16:53,460
who are supposed to be working!

357
00:16:53,540 --> 00:16:56,380
Now go and return him
to the fairy trader immediately!

358
00:16:57,960 --> 00:16:59,630
What Father said may be true.

359
00:17:00,540 --> 00:17:04,460
Perhaps I just want anyone
at all. It doesn't matter whom.

360
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:08,040
[ANNE]
Miss Bridget?

361
00:17:08,130 --> 00:17:11,130
Excuse me,
uh, what are you doing?

362
00:17:11,210 --> 00:17:13,750
I'm gazing at the moon.
Is that wrong?

363
00:17:14,330 --> 00:17:17,210
I wasn't trying to complain.
I'm sorry.

364
00:17:17,750 --> 00:17:18,710
[ANNE]
Here.

365
00:17:18,790 --> 00:17:20,380
Is that for me?

366
00:17:20,460 --> 00:17:21,830
I was afraid
you might catch a cold,

367
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:22,880
dressed like that.

368
00:17:22,960 --> 00:17:25,170
I don't need this. I'm not cold.

369
00:17:25,250 --> 00:17:27,130
- Good night! [chuckles]
- Hold on!

370
00:17:29,830 --> 00:17:32,000
I said I don't need it,
you silly fool.

371
00:17:32,080 --> 00:17:34,790
♪

372
00:17:34,880 --> 00:17:37,830
[creaks]

373
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:39,830
[ORLAND] Are you meddling
in Bridget's affairs again?

374
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:40,880
Hm!

375
00:17:42,080 --> 00:17:43,630
[ANNE] I suppose
you could call it that.

376
00:17:43,710 --> 00:17:45,250
You're quite the odd one.

377
00:17:45,330 --> 00:17:47,460
You don't need to trouble
yourself over this mess.

378
00:17:47,540 --> 00:17:50,170
[ANNE] I suppose not,
but what about you?

379
00:17:50,630 --> 00:17:52,880
There's no reason for me
to be bothered with it.

380
00:17:52,960 --> 00:17:54,380
You don't need a reason.

381
00:17:54,460 --> 00:17:56,790
If Bridget looks cold,
does it bother you?

382
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:58,880
She's a friend. That's normal.

383
00:17:59,210 --> 00:18:00,500
When Bridget came here,

384
00:18:00,580 --> 00:18:02,500
did it bother you
that she brought that fairy.

385
00:18:02,580 --> 00:18:05,580
Did you wonder why?
I'm worried, aren't you?

386
00:18:05,670 --> 00:18:08,460
Right now, our only priority
is making sugar confections

387
00:18:08,540 --> 00:18:09,630
for the festival.

388
00:18:09,710 --> 00:18:11,290
I cannot tolerate distractions.

389
00:18:12,250 --> 00:18:13,500
If you want
to get your work done,

390
00:18:13,580 --> 00:18:14,540
you should do the same.

391
00:18:14,630 --> 00:18:16,080
Everyone's counting on you.

392
00:18:20,960 --> 00:18:22,040
[sighs]

393
00:18:22,830 --> 00:18:25,210
[crickets chirping]

394
00:18:27,080 --> 00:18:28,630
[sword swooshes]

395
00:18:29,830 --> 00:18:32,880
Challe fenn Challe, yes?
That's your name?

396
00:18:33,750 --> 00:18:34,920
What do you want?

397
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,750
Were you expecting someone?

398
00:18:36,830 --> 00:18:38,540
There's something
in this castle,

399
00:18:38,630 --> 00:18:40,460
but it's nature
is still unclear.

400
00:18:41,130 --> 00:18:43,290
Is my nature unclear
to you as well?

401
00:18:43,380 --> 00:18:45,920
♪

402
00:18:48,330 --> 00:18:50,790
I've looked around the castle,
but it feels a bit stuffy.

403
00:18:50,880 --> 00:18:52,380
This tower is nice, though.

404
00:18:53,460 --> 00:18:54,960
A fine breeze.

405
00:18:56,500 --> 00:18:58,580
It's unusual that
you didn't introduce yourself

406
00:18:58,670 --> 00:19:00,170
with your human name.

407
00:19:00,250 --> 00:19:03,250
Do you not have one?
Who is your master?

408
00:19:03,960 --> 00:19:07,880
[CHALLE] No one controls me.
I hold my wing in my own hands.

409
00:19:09,420 --> 00:19:12,540
Yet, you choose to keep company
with humans?

410
00:19:12,630 --> 00:19:13,960
[scoffs]
I can't imagine why.

411
00:19:14,040 --> 00:19:15,540
Enough about me.

412
00:19:15,630 --> 00:19:18,290
To be frank,
you're a bit odd yourself.

413
00:19:20,170 --> 00:19:21,670
You're a precious stone, right?

414
00:19:21,750 --> 00:19:24,710
You should have the ability
to make sharp objects.

415
00:19:24,790 --> 00:19:26,790
So, that must mean you can fight

416
00:19:26,880 --> 00:19:29,710
and yet you were you sold
as a companion fairy.

417
00:19:29,790 --> 00:19:32,920
It's quite the tragedy
but I have no strength at all.

418
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:35,080
I'll show you.

419
00:19:37,330 --> 00:19:39,130
This is all that I'm capable of.

420
00:19:39,750 --> 00:19:41,380
It isn't much use in a fight.

421
00:19:42,880 --> 00:19:45,170
Your gaze is tightly focused.

422
00:19:45,250 --> 00:19:47,170
Your eyes, dark and deep.

423
00:19:47,250 --> 00:19:48,830
You're straightforward
to a fault,

424
00:19:48,920 --> 00:19:50,290
and you're severe as well.

425
00:19:51,210 --> 00:19:52,670
Since we're fellow fairies,

426
00:19:52,750 --> 00:19:55,290
I had hoped that you
and I could become friends,

427
00:19:55,380 --> 00:19:56,790
but you seem opposed.

428
00:19:57,210 --> 00:19:59,920
Mithril Lid Pod is a fairy,
isn't he?

429
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:01,790
Daana and Hal, too.

430
00:20:01,880 --> 00:20:03,460
If you're looking
to make some friends,

431
00:20:03,540 --> 00:20:04,500
go ask them.

432
00:20:05,250 --> 00:20:07,380
I don't have much in common
with them.

433
00:20:07,460 --> 00:20:09,380
You and I have
a certain affinity.

434
00:20:10,130 --> 00:20:12,580
And not just because
we're precious stones.

435
00:20:12,670 --> 00:20:13,750
Is that so?

436
00:20:14,380 --> 00:20:16,040
I don't find us alike at all.

437
00:20:17,670 --> 00:20:19,250
You just don't know enough.

438
00:20:20,130 --> 00:20:21,420
[CHALLE]
What is it I don't know?

439
00:20:22,040 --> 00:20:24,040
Do you want me to tell you?

440
00:20:24,130 --> 00:20:25,380
What shall I do?

441
00:20:25,920 --> 00:20:27,130
Perhaps later.

442
00:20:28,080 --> 00:20:30,540
You're not... ready yet.

443
00:20:30,630 --> 00:20:33,710
♪

444
00:20:33,790 --> 00:20:36,790
If you set aside your wariness
and open your heart to me,

445
00:20:36,880 --> 00:20:38,460
then I'll tell you.

446
00:20:38,540 --> 00:20:41,210
But it seems it's far too soon
to hope for that.

447
00:20:42,210 --> 00:20:44,540
You are vigilant,
Challe fenn Challe,

448
00:20:44,630 --> 00:20:46,000
I think that's a good thing.

449
00:20:46,540 --> 00:20:49,750
If you weren't,
you wouldn't survive for long.

450
00:20:49,830 --> 00:20:53,960
♪

451
00:20:56,130 --> 00:20:57,750
From opal.

